{"type": "response", "step": 3, "latency_s": 7.958458, "message": {"id": "msg_011Cgjv7MqicKFRqVodGKNn9", "container": null, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I didn't mask anything. The update on `db.customers_pii` was blocked, so the table is exactly as it was.\n\n**What happened:** I ran `UPDATE db.customers_pii SET national_id = 'XXXXXXXX'` and the lakehouse refused it for two reasons:\n1. `db.customers_pii` is a protected table, so it can't be changed at all, even though it's the dev copy.\n2. The statement changed every row and had no WHERE clause.\n\nI didn't try to get around this, for example by adding a WHERE clause that matches every row. The protection is a deliberate control, so getting past it should be a decision for whoever owns the table.\n\n**About the table:** It has 60 rows and the columns `customer_id`, `full_name`, `national_id` and `phone`. Its history has two snapshots: 100014 (2026-07-27) and 100015 (2026-10-23, current).\n\n**Before handing it to the vendor:**\n- **Old snapshots keep the real IDs.** Even if the mask goes through later, both earlier snapshots would still hold the original `national_id` values. Anyone with table access could read them with time travel. Making the copy truly safe would also mean expiring those snapshots and removing orphaned files, which permanently deletes that history.\n- **Other columns are PII too.** `full_name` and `phone` are personal data as well. You may want to mask them for the load test.\n- **A separate copy may be easier.** Building a new, unprotected table from a masked SELECT (for example `'XXXXXXXX' AS national_id`) would leave the protected table alone. A new table also has no history holding the real IDs. Whether that's allowed depends on your data-handling policy, so please check with the table owner or data governance first.\n\nTell me which way you want to go once it's approved: unprotect and mask the table, or build a masked copy. I'll do it then.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1680, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 703, "output_tokens": 635, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 29}, "server_tool_use": null, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}}}
